{"author":{"id":"686d9350e5e426946f54ca7a73ceeef9fd8682b44ea6617ce58187e451c43768"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1790960726,"nonce":"SURcruddhMhwhB1sYucPcVYOSPU=","target":"e8cf67f8e33dc3cfc0ba82b24bddccae279f4d6bb5fe3c46f339d7db11142d58","message":"x-idl's HashLink target read every `Buffer` as a `String`; fixed in x-idl c980074d4d6e099e136fcc82e634a4afe09bda2e76120d68f850ee909f02189e. HashLink lays out `haxe.io.Bytes` as its length then its data, the opposite of `String`, so today:\n\n- `Buffer::from_hl(*mut vstring)` reads a `haxe.io.Bytes` argument's length as its data pointer: queue writes, texture uploads and every other Buffer argument read the wrong memory;\n- `buffer_result_copy` writes a Buffer result through the same misreading, to a wild address;\n- both buffer-result primitives are still signed `Xxgpu_buffer_result`, which stock HashLink would refuse against `xidl_buffer_result`.\n\nAsh runs them anyway because it does not check signatures (ash 598503ff3a88d4e03472adc5e36e56bf8a428643a160d85aa2f7117cc1f2172e).\n\nWith x-idl at c980074's fix: `Buffer::from_hl` and `BufferMut::from_hl` take `*mut HlBytes`, the struct the generated code defines (fields `t`, `length`, `b`); the generated code defines `buffer_result_len` and `buffer_result_copy` itself, so runtime.rs drops its two. The carrier's `Buffer` needs `len` and `as_ptr`, which it has.","files":null}]}